[[:db/retract 17592186118163 :answer-field/choices 17592186118167] {:db/id 17592186119810 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-fa3eae70-d536-57c6-818d-d88d2dc98925"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119621 :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Col}(B),$ we need to check if the equation $B\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[B \\,|\\, \\mathbf{b}]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[B\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 15 & -6 & 21 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=7 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get the true statement $0=0.$ So the system is equivalent to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=7 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $x_2=0.$ Substituting into the first equation gives $x_1=\\dfrac 7 5.$ \n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $B\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent, which implies that $\\mathbf{b}\\in\\textrm{Col}(B).$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $\\mathbf{b}$ as a linear combination of $\\mathbf{b}_1$ and $\\mathbf{b}_2\\mathbin{:}$\n![](images/8a/8a35321d3a29ee86c5af54e23dabd8d3ac93bf7831981507dff3e501796f96a7.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119855 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1df900d6-620c-58af-b345-1b8940d52367"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119670 :question/worked-solution "If $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Col}(A),$ then the equation $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A \\,|\\, \\mathbf{b}]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2+k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -32 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2+k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -32 \\\\ 0 & -11 & k-48\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{8}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -11 & k-48\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+11{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=10 \\\\ {x}_{2}=4 \\\\ 0=k-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=k-4,$ which means that $k=4.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119811 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6e653566-d375-5ee1-b745-3dfd829381b0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119622 :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Col}(C),$ we need to check if the equation $C\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[C \\,|\\, \\mathbf{b}]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[C\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}=5 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ 5{x}_{3}=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $x_3=1$. Substituting into the second equation gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{2}+4(1) & =1 \\\\ 3{x}_{2} & =-3 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, from the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =5-{x}_{2}-4{x}_{3} \\\\  & =5-(-1)-4(1) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $C\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent, which implies that $\\mathbf{b}\\in\\textrm{Col}(C).$ \n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $\\mathbf{b}$ as a linear combination of $\\mathbf{c}_1,$ $\\mathbf{c}_2,$ and $\\mathbf{c}_3\\mathbin{:}$\n![](images/4c/4cccd67d5e043d72e0b6949543883e6187d9ef807b7a470146628cbadf7eead7.svg)\n\nFinally, we get $x_1 \\cdot x_2 \\cdot x_3 = 2 \\cdot (-1) \\cdot 1 = -2$." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120339 :question/problem "The matrix $H$ and the vector $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(H).$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$, where ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{h}_{1}+{x}_{2}{h}_{2},$ and ${h}_{1},$ ${h}_{2}$ are the respective columns of $H.$\n\n$$\nH=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(H),$ we need to check if the equation $Hx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[H\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[H\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=7 \\\\ {x}_{2}=2 \\\\ 0=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get the false statement $0=-2.$ \n\nTherefore, the system is inconsistent, which implies that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(H).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186118163 :answer-field/correct "answer-a4e728bc-a0d7-5941-ae7e-43acb5d00189" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a4e728bc-a0d7-5941-ae7e-43acb5d00189"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a4e728bc-a0d7-5941-ae7e-43acb5d00189" :answer/id #uuid "a4e728bc-a0d7-5941-ae7e-43acb5d00189" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(H)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-fa3eae70-d536-57c6-818d-d88d2dc98925" :question/id #uuid "fa3eae70-d536-57c6-818d-d88d2dc98925" :question/math-academy-id "q-110965" :question/problem "The matrix $K$ and the vector $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(K).$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ where ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{k}_{1}+{x}_{2}{k}_{2},$ and ${k}_{1},$ ${k}_{2}$ are the respective columns of $K.$\n\n$$\nK=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(K),$ we need to check if the equation $Kx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[K\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[K\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 0=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get the false statement $0=3.$  \n\nTherefore, the system is inconsistent, which implies that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(K).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fa9df3d7-3177-5d86-afd1-6157ae9530cb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fa9df3d7-3177-5d86-afd1-6157ae9530cb" :answer-field/id #uuid "fa9df3d7-3177-5d86-afd1-6157ae9530cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-abc883cc-1645-5165-aa94-e26727b22c02" :answer-field/choices ["answer-093c0e17-b9d7-5361-b0f1-495edfe1ed11" "answer-6c9a2490-6ff3-538d-b8fc-292a428032fc" "answer-cc637fff-6c90-5ccd-9438-8fa331c95ad6" "answer-9a2ac221-6a8f-511f-bdab-4c58f95296f8" "answer-abc883cc-1645-5165-aa94-e26727b22c02"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-093c0e17-b9d7-5361-b0f1-495edfe1ed11" :answer/id #uuid "093c0e17-b9d7-5361-b0f1-495edfe1ed11" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6c9a2490-6ff3-538d-b8fc-292a428032fc" :answer/id #uuid "6c9a2490-6ff3-538d-b8fc-292a428032fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cc637fff-6c90-5ccd-9438-8fa331c95ad6" :answer/id #uuid "cc637fff-6c90-5ccd-9438-8fa331c95ad6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9a2ac221-6a8f-511f-bdab-4c58f95296f8" :answer/id #uuid "9a2ac221-6a8f-511f-bdab-4c58f95296f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-abc883cc-1645-5165-aa94-e26727b22c02" :answer/id #uuid "abc883cc-1645-5165-aa94-e26727b22c02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(K)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1df900d6-620c-58af-b345-1b8940d52367" :question/id #uuid "1df900d6-620c-58af-b345-1b8940d52367" :question/math-academy-id "q-110981" :question/problem "Consider the matrix given by $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}-20 \\\\ -14 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to $\\text{Col}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "If $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(A),$ then the equation $Ax=b$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -20 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -14 \\\\ -1 & 1 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -20 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -14 \\\\ 0 & 4 & k-20\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -20 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -14 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=-20 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}=-14 \\\\ 0=k+8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=k+8,$ which means that $k=-8.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-35749f45-4831-5cfb-b5cd-f36d9fb901de"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-35749f45-4831-5cfb-b5cd-f36d9fb901de" :answer-field/id #uuid "35749f45-4831-5cfb-b5cd-f36d9fb901de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6b2ca576-5a4b-51b9-8394-245a07fc1667" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6b2ca576-5a4b-51b9-8394-245a07fc1667" "answer-80756020-169b-5fd6-8215-6076a6443964" "answer-909a8f13-1f9a-5602-b685-461ec6c51d98" "answer-2dcf3ee9-518e-59ca-a87d-eb7fff848801" "answer-25070fd0-c7a7-5aad-88d7-0112a5cceca4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6b2ca576-5a4b-51b9-8394-245a07fc1667" :answer/id #uuid "6b2ca576-5a4b-51b9-8394-245a07fc1667" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-80756020-169b-5fd6-8215-6076a6443964" :answer/id #uuid "80756020-169b-5fd6-8215-6076a6443964" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-909a8f13-1f9a-5602-b685-461ec6c51d98" :answer/id #uuid "909a8f13-1f9a-5602-b685-461ec6c51d98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2dcf3ee9-518e-59ca-a87d-eb7fff848801" :answer/id #uuid "2dcf3ee9-518e-59ca-a87d-eb7fff848801" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-25070fd0-c7a7-5aad-88d7-0112a5cceca4" :answer/id #uuid "25070fd0-c7a7-5aad-88d7-0112a5cceca4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186247191 :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(C),$ we need to check if the equation $Cx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[C\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[C\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 3 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 & -12 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 3 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 & -12 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 & -14\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 3 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 & -12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-8 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=-12 \\\\ 5{x}_{3}=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=2.$ Substituting it into the second equation gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2}-(2) & =-12 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, from the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =-8-3{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} \\\\  & =-8-3(-5)-3(2) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $Cx=b$ is consistent, which implies that $b\\in \\text{Col}(C).$ \n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${c}_{1},$ ${c}_{2},$ and ${c}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -12 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}=1\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{c}_{1}}+(-5)\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{c}_{2}}+2\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{c}_{3}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}=1\\cdot (-5)\\cdot 2=-10.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-6e653566-d375-5ee1-b745-3dfd829381b0" :question/id #uuid "6e653566-d375-5ee1-b745-3dfd829381b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-111042" :question/problem "The matrix $C$ and the vector $b$ are given below.\nDetermine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(C).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}$, where ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}+{x}_{3}{c}_{3},$ and ${c}_{1}$, ${c}_{2}$, and ${c}_{3}$ are the respective columns of $C.$\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(C),$ we need to check if the equation $Cx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[C\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[C\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & -4 & 9 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & ↔{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -4 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -4 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -7 & -16 & -11\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(\\frac{7}{3}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -9 & -18\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=5 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-3 \\\\ -9{x}_{3}=-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=2.$ Substituting it into the second equation gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{2}+3(2) & =-3 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, from the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =5-2{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} \\\\  & =5-2(-3)-3(2) \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $Cx=b$ is consistent, which implies that $b\\in \\text{Col}(C).$ \n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${c}_{1},$ ${c}_{2},$ and ${c}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}=5\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{c}_{1}}+(-3)\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{c}_{2}}+2\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{c}_{3}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}=5\\cdot (-3)\\cdot 2=-30.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-936859a3-a75e-5199-89df-699c1acfd3b4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-936859a3-a75e-5199-89df-699c1acfd3b4" :answer-field/id #uuid "936859a3-a75e-5199-89df-699c1acfd3b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3bb23460-0309-50b0-9f56-6030ff2b9177" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7c7bc9e5-99a0-5450-9994-235495344319" "answer-3bb23460-0309-50b0-9f56-6030ff2b9177" "answer-9c2abbdd-3e2c-554e-8306-7b4a584274a0" "answer-33644fcb-15fc-5a07-8b9c-fcbe4057fb01" "answer-1828c4ca-eb5d-5389-aec1-1f80b5436666"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7c7bc9e5-99a0-5450-9994-235495344319" :answer/id #uuid "7c7bc9e5-99a0-5450-9994-235495344319" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-28" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3bb23460-0309-50b0-9f56-6030ff2b9177" :answer/id #uuid "3bb23460-0309-50b0-9f56-6030ff2b9177" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9c2abbdd-3e2c-554e-8306-7b4a584274a0" :answer/id #uuid "9c2abbdd-3e2c-554e-8306-7b4a584274a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-33644fcb-15fc-5a07-8b9c-fcbe4057fb01" :answer/id #uuid "33644fcb-15fc-5a07-8b9c-fcbe4057fb01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1828c4ca-eb5d-5389-aec1-1f80b5436666" :answer/id #uuid "1828c4ca-eb5d-5389-aec1-1f80b5436666" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(C)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121037 :tutorial/content "The **column space** of a matrix $A$ is denoted $\\text{Col}(A)$ and is the span of the columns of $A$ (i.e., the set of all possible linear combinations of columns of $A$). For example, consider the matrix\n\n![](images/6c/6c03ab3dfd7b75c9a89defe102f33946da200fb88d26139e54c889a90467068a.svg)\nwhere we denote its columns by $\\color{red}\\mathbf{a}_1$ and ${\\color{blue}\\mathbf{a}_2},$ respectively. The column space of this matrix is given by\n![](images/5f/5faad23bc77f821d42223beaca06364e38c7f0ba8a4869cb138e0e923e90b8f7.svg)\n\nNow, suppose we would like to determine whether the vector ![](images/45/45349edee356334c54ad85a6d60757a6a7833a392962086815a2436446e323dc.svg) lies in $\\textrm{Col}(A).$ In other words, we need to check if $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Span}\\{ {\\color{red}\\mathbf{a}_1}, {\\color{blue}\\mathbf{a}_2} \\}.$ So, we need to determine whether $\\mathbf{b}$ can be written as some linear combination of $\\color{red}\\mathbf{a}_1$ and ${\\color{blue}\\mathbf{a}_2}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the equation above can be written as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =b \\\\ {{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{x}} & ={{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{b}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation is equivalent to $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}.$ To solve the equation, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A \\,|\\, \\mathbf{b}]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -7 & -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ -7{x}_{2}=-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $x_2=1.$ Substituting into the first equation, we get $x_1=-1.$\n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent, which implies that $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Col}(A).$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $\\mathbf{b}$ as a linear combination of $\\color{red}\\mathbf{a}_1$ and ${\\color{blue}\\mathbf{a}_2}\\mathbin{:}$\n![](images/a3/a3965a53b3b3cfda2e11c4a68ba882631dc2763f32de67de30b4751aca76f2e5.svg)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]}]
